# Frontend

- React + TypeScript + Vite + TailwindCSS + ECharts.
- Professional quant-terminal aesthetic. Dark and light themes are first-class.
- Every list supports search, filter, sort, pagination.
- Source status, data quality, and UNKNOWN fields must be visible. Never fill blanks with fake numbers.
- Recommendations must show explanation, risk, confidence, and invalidation.
- Distinguish model recommendation vs user action vs actual result in every tracking view.
- Do not call vendor APIs from the browser. All data goes through the local backend.
- Portfolio PnL must show Gross PnL, Total Cost, Net PnL, ROI — including fees, funding, gas, slippage where recorded.
